 <!--
-Post checklist (delete before publishing):
-1. One idea per post. If you need "and also", that is post #2.
-2. Structure: what it is -> why it matters -> how it works -> try it yourself -> references.
-3. Every claim gets a link or your own experiment. No unsourced numbers.
-4. Read it out loud once. Cut 20%.
+Delete this comment before publishing.
+
+SHAPE. Pick one.
+  research / experiment:  the finding -> why the usual view misses it -> what we measured (short)
+                          -> what happened -> what I'd test next -> paper/code links
+  explainer / build-log:  what it is -> one concrete example -> why it is hard -> what actually helps
+                          -> further reading
+
+RULES.
+  1. One idea per post. If you need "and also", that is the next post.
+  2. First paragraph: the point, in plain words. No "in this post I will".
+  3. Every number has a link to where it comes from. Every claim has a source or your own experiment.
+  4. Define a term in a clause the first time it appears. No glossary section.
+  5. Depth goes in a collapse block:  {{</* collapse summary="Details for the curious" */>}} ... {{</* /collapse */>}}
+  6. Say what you expected before you say what happened. Keep the failures in.
+  7. End research posts with a section named exactly "What I would test next".
+  8. Read it aloud once. Cut 20%.
+
+FIGURES (house style, same on every post).
+  Palette:  accent #1f6f8b (the thing we care about) | gray #8a8a8a (baseline, context) | warm #d1495b (attack, blocked, bad)
+  Charts:   matplotlib, transparent background, no top/right spines, labels in plain words, one message per chart,
+            export SVG or PNG 1600px wide.
+  Diagrams: clean SVG (one tool for the whole blog).
+  Every figure uses the shortcode so it gets alt text and a caption that says what to see:
+    {{</* figure src="fig-1.png" alt="..." caption="..." */>}}
+  Tables: only to compare, never wider than five columns, never copied from a PDF.
 -->
diff --git a/assets/css/extended/custom.css b/assets/css/extended/custom.css
index 830eeec..d6e0e4e 100644
--- a/assets/css/extended/custom.css
+++ b/assets/css/extended/custom.css
@@ -1,13 +1,27 @@
-/* Readability tweaks on top of PaperMod — keep this file small. */
+/* Readability tweaks on top of PaperMod. Keep this file small: if it passes ~30 lines,
+   ask what problem each rule solves. */
 
-/* Slightly wider measure for technical posts with code blocks */
+/* One accent color, used for links only. Muted so it reads on light and dark. */
+:root { --accent: #1f6f8b; }
+:root[data-theme="dark"] { --accent: #6fb3c9; }
+.post-content a:not(.anchor) { color: var(--accent); text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
+.post-content a:not(.anchor):hover { text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
+
+/* Body text: a little more air for long technical posts */
 .post-content { line-height: 1.75; }
 
+/* Figure captions: small, muted, centered. The caption says what to see in the figure. */
+.post-content figure > figcaption { font-weight: normal; font-size: 15px; color: var(--secondary); text-align: center; }
+.post-content figure > figcaption > p { font-size: 15px; }
+
+/* Callout: a blockquote is the only callout style on this site. Use for "note" and
+   "if you only read one thing". Not for quoting people (plain italics do that). */
+.post-content blockquote { border-inline-start: 0.25rem solid var(--accent); background: var(--code-bg); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: var(--radius); }
+.post-content blockquote p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
+
 /* Tables: PaperMod default is cramped for benchmark-style tables */
 .post-content table { display: block; overflow-x: auto; white-space: nowrap; }
 .post-content th, .post-content td { padding: 6px 12px; }
 
 /* Inline code: a touch more contrast */
 .post-content code { padding: 2px 5px; border-radius: 4px; }
